{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HxWZN8B3rcjRF3pKYkDiCc","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t\"\"\"\n2\tSICA end-to-end pipeline: trace generation -> constraint extraction -> Z3 dedup -> MAX-SAT -> scoring -> answer selection.\n3\tInput: problem dict with \"problem\" and \"answer\" fields\n4\tOutput: result dict with answer, score, constraint stats, maxsat stats\n5\tDependencies: trace_generator, constraint_extractor, z3_maxsat, scorer\n6\t\"\"\"\n7\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n8\t\n9\timport logging\n10\timport time\n11\tfrom collections import Counter\n12\t\n13\tfrom .trace_generator import TraceGenerator\n14\tfrom .constraint_extractor import ConstraintExtractor\n15\tfrom .z3_maxsat import ConstraintDeduplicator, MaxSATSolver\n16\tfrom .scorer import InvariantScorer\n17\t\n18\tlogger = logging.getLogger(__name__)\n19\t\n20\t\n21\tclass SICAPipeline:\n22\t    def __init__(\n23\t        self,\n24\t        trace_generator: TraceGenerator,\n25\t        constraint_extractor: ConstraintExtractor,\n26\t        k: int = 12,\n27\t        maxsat_timeout_ms: int = 10000,\n28\t    ):\n29\t        self.trace_generator = trace_generator\n30\t        self.constraint_extractor = constraint_extractor\n31\t        self.k = k\n32\t        self.deduplicator = ConstraintDeduplicator()\n33\t        self.solver = MaxSATSolver()\n34\t        self.scorer = InvariantScorer()\n35\t        self.maxsat_timeout_ms = maxsat_timeout_ms\n36\t\n37\t    def run_single(self, problem: dict) -> dict:\n38\t        \"\"\"Run full SICA pipeline on a single problem.\"\"\"\n39\t        t_start = time.perf_counter()\n40\t\n41\t        # 1. Generate K traces\n42\t        t0 = time.perf_counter()\n43\t        traces = self.trace_generator.generate(problem[\"problem\"], k=self.k)\n44\t        trace_time = time.perf_counter() - t0\n45\t\n46\t        # 2. Extract constraints from each trace (batch for concurrency)\n47\t        t0 = time.perf_counter()\n48\t        all_constraints = self.constraint_extractor.extract_batch(\n49\t            [t[\"trace\"] for t in traces]\n50\t        )\n51\t        extract_time = time.perf_counter() - t0\n52\t\n53\t        total_constraints = sum(len(c) for c in all_constraints)\n54\t        non_empty = sum(1 for c in all_constraints if c)\n55\t\n56\t        # 3. Deduplicate via z3 equivalence\n57\t        t0 = time.perf_counter()\n58\t        unique_constraints = self.deduplicator.deduplicate(all_constraints)\n59\t        dedup_time = time.perf_counter() - t0\n60\t\n61\t        # 4. MAX-SAT solve\n62\t        t0 = time.perf_counter()\n63\t        maxsat_result = self.solver.solve(unique_constraints, timeout_ms=self.maxsat_timeout_ms)\n64\t        maxsat_time = time.perf_counter() - t0\n65\t\n66\t        # 5. Score candidates\n67\t        candidates = list(set(t[\"answer\"] for t in traces if t[\"answer\"]))\n68\t        answer_counts = Counter(t[\"answer\"] for t in traces if t[\"answer\"])\n69\t        scores = self.scorer.score(maxsat_result, traces, candidates)\n70\t        selected = self.scorer.select_answer(scores, answer_counts)\n71\t\n72\t        total_time = time.perf_counter() - t_start\n73\t\n74\t        return {\n75\t            \"answer\": selected,\n76\t            \"scores\": scores,\n77\t            \"answer_counts\": dict(answer_counts),\n78\t            \"traces\": traces,\n79\t            \"constraints_stats\": {\n80\t                \"total_extracted\": total_constraints,\n81\t                \"traces_with_constraints\": non_empty,\n82\t                \"unique_after_dedup\": len(unique_constraints),\n83\t            },\n84\t            \"maxsat_stats\": {\n85\t                \"satisfied\": len(maxsat_result.satisfied),\n86\t                \"excluded\": len(maxsat_result.excluded),\n87\t                \"total_weight\": maxsat_result.total_weight,\n88\t                \"solve_time_ms\": maxsat_result.solve_time_ms,\n89\t            },\n90\t            \"timing\": {\n91\t                \"trace_gen_s\": round(trace_time, 3),\n92\t                \"extraction_s\": round(extract_time, 3),\n93\t                \"dedup_s\": round(dedup_time, 3),\n94\t                \"maxsat_s\": round(maxsat_time, 3),\n95\t                \"total_s\": round(total_time, 3),\n96\t            },\n97\t        }\n98\t\n99\t    def run_batch(self, problems: list[dict]) -> list[dict]:\n100\t        \"\"\"Run pipeline on a batch of problems.\"\"\"\n101\t        results = []\n102\t        for i, p in enumerate(problems):\n103\t            logger.info(\"Processing problem %d/%d\", i + 1, len(problems))\n104\t            result = self.run_single(p)\n105\t            result[\"problem_idx\"] = i\n106\t            results.append(result)\n107\t        return results\n108\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01KTTtHKEDzmwvFFpx5YDYWD","session_id":"78f4268f-add9-4f5f-97a8-4d696a1c2e4e","uuid":"03611051-51f3-4da5-9677-358b643f255c","timestamp":"2026-05-16T06:20:06.940Z"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Sf6bxMFUnHPNagdtSHbB9S","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"result\":\"{\\\"success\\\": true, \\\"data\\\": {\\\"path\\\": \\\"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0513_3/projects/symb_invariant_consensus/paper_framing.md\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"# Paper Framing — symb_invariant_consensus\\\\n\\\\n## Target Venue\\\\n- Primary: EMNLP 2026 Main (ARR May 25)\\\\n- Fallback: AAAI 2027 (Aug 1)\\\\n- Deadline: May 25, 2026 (ARR submission)\\\\n\\\\n## Core Claims (3 条)\\\\n1. **Principled Tiebreaking**: SICA resolves Self-Consistency voting ties through symbolic constraint weighting, achieving higher accuracy than arbitrary tiebreak rules on logic reasoning benchmarks (FOLIO +6.7pp, combined +3.3pp on 60 questions; target: statistically significant on 200+ questions).\\\\n2. **Operating Regime Characterization**: The effectiveness of symbolic consensus is governed by trace diversity (C0), which tracks epistemic uncertainty — SICA adds value when C0>20% (model uncertain, outputs diverse) but degenerates to SC when C0<5% (model confident, outputs converge). C0 correlates with model architecture (instruction > reasoning) but is not identical to it; it also depends on task difficulty relative to model capability. Validated across 3+ model families (Qwen, Mistral, LLaMA) and 2 reasoning architectures (QwQ, DeepSeek-R1).\\\\n3. **C0 as Practical Diagnostic**: Multi-candidate rate (C0) serves as a zero-cost predictor of whether SICA deployment will yield gains over SC, enabling practitioners to decide without running full symbolic analysis.\\\\n\\\\n## Core Insight\\\\nSymbolic constraint consensus doesn't uniformly improve reasoning — it specifically helps when there IS disagreement to resolve. We provide the first systematic study of WHEN symbolic consensus adds value, revealing that trace diversity (C0) — driven by epistemic uncertainty rather than model family or task domain — determines the operating regime. This transforms SICA from \\\\\\\"yet another ensemble method\\\\\\\" into \\\\\\\"a method with formally characterizable applicability boundaries,\\\\\\\" validated across 3 model families and multiple reasoning domains.\\\\n\\\\n## Story Spine\\\\n- **Problem**: Self-Consistency (SC) aggregates LLM reasoning paths via majority voting but treats all chains as opaque votes, discarding the logical structure within them. When votes are tied, SC falls back to arbitrary rules (alphabetical, random) with no principled resolution.\\\\n- **Existing approaches & gaps**: SC (Wang et al. 2023) — pure voting, no reasoning structure. USC (Chen et al. 2023) — universal SC, still voting-based. None exploit the formal logical structure within reasoning traces for consensus, and none characterize when symbolic methods help vs. don't.\\\\n- **Our framing**: SICA extracts first-order logic constraints from reasoning traces and uses weighted partial MAX-SAT to find the globally consistent answer. We show this provides principled tiebreaking (75%+ win rate on ties vs 25% for SC) but only when trace diversity exists. We formalize this as C0 (multi-candidate rate) — a zero-cost diagnostic that tracks epistemic uncertainty — and validate across 3 model families (Qwen, Mistral, LLaMA), 2 reasoning architectures (QwQ, DeepSeek-R1), and multiple domains (logic, math).\\\\n- **Headline result template**: \\\\\\\"On FOLIO, SICA achieves 80.0% vs SC's 73.3% (+6.7pp) with Qwen2.5-14B-Instruct. On the same benchmarks with QwQ-32B, SICA degenerates to SC (C0=3.6%), revealing that symbolic consensus effectiveness is governed by trace diversity, not task difficulty.\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns & Defensive Experiments\\\\n1. **\\\\\\\"Gains not statistically significant\\\\\\\"** → exp-001: Expand to 804 questions for statistical power\\\\n2. **\\\\\\\"Only a better tiebreaker, not worth the overhead\\\\\\\"** → exp-002: K sensitivity; exp-009: overhead analysis (P1); exp-013: constraint ablation (MaxSAT vs count-only vs random-weight)\\\\n3. **\\\\\\\"Only Qwen models — family-specific artifact?\\\\\\\"** → exp-010: Mistral-7B + exp-011: LLaMA-8B (3-family validation)\\\\n4. **\\\\\\\"Only one reasoning model\\\\\\\"** → exp-014: DeepSeek-R1-Distill-7B (second reasoning architecture)\\\\n5. **\\\\\\\"Only logic domain — restricted answer space\\\\\\\"** → exp-012: GSM8K pilot with 14B (cross-domain C0 test)\\\\n6. **\\\\\\\"ProofWriter shows 0pp gain\\\\\\\"** → Domain analysis in exp-001 expanded results\\\\n7. **\\\\\\\"Random tiebreak baseline closes the gap\\\\\\\"** → exp-003: Direct SICA vs SC-random vs SC-deterministic comparison (done on D012, will re-run on expanded)\\\\n8. **\\\\\\\"Why not just use a reasoning model?\\\\\\\"** → exp-005: QwQ-32B + exp-014: DeepSeek-R1 show reasoning models are self-consistent → SICA redundant; instruction models (cheaper, more deployed) benefit\\\\n9. **\\\\\\\"MAX-SAT is over-engineering\\\\\\\"** → exp-013: Constraint ablation proves satisfiability checking adds value over simple counting\\\\n10. **\\\\\\\"Within-family scaling?\\\\\\\"** → exp-004: 7B + exp-007: 72B-AWQ show C0 trend within Qwen family\\\\n\\\\n## Venue Fit Risks\\\\n- EMNLP: Contribution may feel narrow if framed as ONLY tiebreaking. Primary intellectual contribution is the \\\\\\\"operating regime characterization\\\\\\\" — the tiebreaking mechanism is evidence, not the claim.\\\\n- Cross-discipline: Combines formal logic (MAX-SAT) with NLP (LLM reasoning). MAX-SAT needs clear explanation for NLP audience.\\\\n- Negative results: QwQ-32B data must be presented as insight (\\\\\\\"When Does Symbolic Consensus Degenerate?\\\\\\\"), not failure.\\\\n- Statistical power: 60-question results are fragile. 200+ question expansion is prerequisite for credible submission.\\\\n\\\", \\\"total_chars\\\": 5168, \\\"truncated\\\": false}, \\\"error\\\": null, \\\"metadata\\\": {}}\"}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01UT1eKrN3KQV3nY7LVbCMHd","session_id":"78f4268f-add9-4f5f-97a8-4d696a1c2e4e","uuid":"4ef01b45-ca3f-4604-b566-424e7f1d1f53","timestamp":"2026-05-16T06:20:06.551Z"}
